# Apply a poison vial to a non-weapon item, whose handler prints its own line
# and returns NOTHING; the y-menu fallback must NOT add a second line. Read by
# tools/check_yuse_no_effect.sh, bd inc-k8uw.
#
# The orc barbarian's kit holds no vial, so the vial is made in wizard mode.
# Neither chargen nor the standard class kits give a small glass vial to a
# non-evil character (lib/classes.irh gives one only to an EVIL actor), so the
# wizard route is used: [w] enters wizard mode, [y] confirms the first time and
# opens the menu, "Item Acquisition" opens the browser. Item Acquisition does
# not currently work through tools/check_yuse_activate.sh because its scripted
# @until target name is stale, but the browser itself works; see that check's
# header for the general shape.
#
# The browser draws its candidates in the message window with the selected row
# in the middle and NO menu letters, so @until walks DOWN until the wanted name
# appears at the bottom row, then one more DOWN moves the selection onto it.
# The glyph strip is walked RIGHT*35 to the Tools category (T_TOOL,
# ItemGlyphs[src/Tables.cpp:320]); the header line names the category, and
# after-apply reads the handler's own words, so a miscount shows up as a run
# that never held the vial rather than as a false pass.
#
# GETTING IT INTO THE PACK. The acquisition auto-stows the vial, but on this
# build it first lands on the floor: the after-apply oracle only means
# something if the vial is in hand, so the script [g]ets it (opening Inventory
# Mode with it In the Air) and drops it into the Ready Hand with [a].
#
# THE VERB IS APPLY, whose handler is lib/mundane.irh:1016. Applying the vial
# to a non-weapon, non-missile item reaches "You can only poison weapons and
# ammunition." and returns NOTHING. Before the guard the y-menu fallback then
# printed a second line, "The loincloth cannot be applied."; after the guard
# only the handler's line is on the screen.

@include chargen.keys

# --- acquire a small glass vial --------------------------------------------
w
y
@choose "Item Acquisition"
RIGHT*35
@until "Small glass vial" DOWN
DOWN
ENTER
@while "In the Air':small glass" s
@while "Ready Hand" ESC
@dump:acquired
g
@while "In the Air':small glass" a

# --- apply it to the loincloth ---------------------------------------------
y
@choose "Apply"
@choose "small glass vial"
i
@choose "loincloth"
@dump:after-apply
@quit
